  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FeSL uses the XACML 2.0 hierchical resource profile.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This means that an incoming PID is converted to a set of XACML resource IDs, including both the PID itself and the hierarchical path to the pid.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The FedoraRIAttributeFinder attempts to locate attribute values based on all of the resource IDs - so when it attempts this based on a hierarchical path, an exception is found as the resource is not a valid Fedora PID.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This results in failure of policy evaluation.  (\"indeterminate\").",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The attribute finder should only attempt to find attributes for valid Fedora subjects, ie PIDs and DSIDs, and should return an empty bag for anything else.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
