     "body": "<p>Figured out why this was working in Muradora and not in FeSL - in Muradora the code goes through RelationshipResolverHttpImpl, which contains code to examine the path and figure out the correct Fedora resource identifier (pid, pid/ds) from the hierarchical resource path.</p>\n\n<p>In FeSL it goes straight to the relationships methods without any such functionality (it calls the relationship resolver, which assumes a valid Fedora resource identifier).  </p>\n\n<p>The logical place for this splitting is within the attribute finder module.</p>",
     "created": "21/Dec/10 8:16 PM",
     "id": "11748",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10801/comment/11748",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
